{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/pulls/1873","id":4993704024,"node_id":"PR_kwDON109P88AAAABKaXgWA","html_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/pull/1873","diff_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/pull/1873.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Vexa-ai/vexa/pull/1873.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1873","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/pulls/1873/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/pulls/1873/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/issues/1873/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Vexa-ai/vexa/statuses/bcf92114662384efce3073f42eef0072e05b3578","number":1873,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"fix(bot): authenticated launches drop --incognito so the restored profile is used (#1725)","user":{"login":"kovacsistvanpeter-stack","id":264636533,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8YIdQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264636533?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack","html_url":"https://github.com/kovacsistvanpeter-stack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"**Delivers issue:** #1725\n\n## Contribution rights (first contribution only)\n\n- [x] **Independent:** I created this contribution, or otherwise have the right to submit it\n  under Apache-2.0, and it is not owned or controlled by an employer, client, or other entity.\n  <!-- rights:independent -->\n- [ ] **Employer/client authorization required:** an employer, client, or other entity owns or\n  may control this contribution. I am requesting Vexa's private corporate-authorization process.\n  <!-- rights:corporate -->\n- [ ] **Unsure:** I need a private rights review before merge.\n  <!-- rights:uncertain -->\n\nThe commit carries a DCO `Signed-off-by` line.\n\n## What and why\n\n`launchBrowser()` in `core/meetings/services/bot/src/capture-bridge.ts` built the launch args as `[...getAuthenticatedBrowserArgs(), ...getJoinBrowserArgs()]`, and `JOIN_BROWSER_ARGS` contains `--incognito`. An incognito context does not read the persistent profile restored from S3, so an authenticated Google Meet bot reaches the lobby as a signed-out guest and fails with `auth_session_missing`, exactly as #1725 describes.\n\nThe change:\n- `browser-args.ts`: `getAuthenticatedJoinBrowserArgs()` returns `getJoinBrowserArgs()` minus `--incognito`, exported from `@vexa/join`.\n- `capture-bridge.ts`: `launchBrowser()` uses it when `inv.authenticated` is set; guest launches keep `getJoinBrowserArgs()` unchanged.\n- New unit test `modules/join/src/__tests__/authenticatedArgs.test.ts`, wired into the join package's `test` script.\n\n## Observation bundle\n\n- **C1, reproduce:** self-hosted v0.12.28 compose stack, `BOT_AUTHENTICATED=true`, a personal Google account signed in through the remote-browser login flow (`provision-cli`, validate: `signedOut=false authCookie=true`). ran: two bot spawns into a Meet the account owns, minutes after a fresh session upload. saw: the S3 restore completed, the lobby showed \"Ask to join\" plus the guest name field, and the bot exited `auth_session_missing` both times.\n- **C2, isolate:** ran: a probe in the same `vexaai/vexa-bot:v0.12.28` image that launches Chromium on a copy of the same profile with the same `--password-store=basic`, once without and once with `--incognito`. saw: without, `myaccount.google.com` is signed in and the Meet lobby offers \"Join now\" with no name field; with `--incognito`, the account page redirects to the signed-out landing and the lobby shows \"Ask to join\" plus the name field. concluded: `--incognito` alone explains the failure. The profile copy (full profile or only the auth-essential subset) is fine.\n- **C3, fix live:** ran: the same stack with the one-line equivalent of this change applied to `dist/capture-bridge.js` in a derived image. saw: \"Located authenticated join CTA via selector: Join now\", \"Successfully admitted to the Google Meet meeting - no waiting room required\"; on stop, `[s3-sync] Uploaded 13 auth-essential items` (write-back works); a second run 4 minutes later also joined signed in.\n\n## Acceptance floor\n\n| Row | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Authenticated launch drops `--incognito` | `authenticatedArgs.test.ts`: \"authenticated launch drops --incognito\" PASS; C3 live run |\n| Guest launch unchanged | test: \"guest launch keeps --incognito\" PASS (also the control that the flag is in the canonical set); `launchBrowser()` uses `getJoinBrowserArgs()` when `inv.authenticated` is not set |\n| No other flag changes | test: \"only --incognito is removed\", \"every other flag is kept, in order\" PASS |\n| Existing join tests | `localePin.test.ts`: 10 passed, 0 failed |\n\nNot covered here, said plainly: the unit test exercises the helper, not the `launchBrowser()` selection itself (a regression of that one line back to `getJoinBrowserArgs()` would not be caught by it). The live run (C3) covers that path. I did not run the bot package's `tsc` build, because the workspace dependencies were not installed in my checkout; the change is two imports and one conditional.\n\n## Docs diff (D6c)\n\nNo docs change: `authenticated-bots.mdx` already describes the intended behaviour (a restored, signed-in profile); this makes the code match it.\n\n## Security checks\n\nNo new dependencies. The diff contains no secrets, URLs or identifiers; secrets scan of the diff: clean.\n\n## Validation request\n\nAnyone running `BOT_AUTHENTICATED=true` with a provisioned Google session: spawn a Meet bot and watch the lobby step. Before: \"Ask to join\" + guest name field, `auth_session_missing`. After: \"Join now\" (or \"Ask to join\" without a name field when not pre-admitted), joined as the account.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-24T08:04:11Z","updated_at":"2026-11-02T17:24:14Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":null,"assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kovacsistvanpeter-stack:fix/authenticated-no-incognito","ref":"fix/authenticated-no-incognito","repo":{"id":1431955965,"node_id":"R_kgDOVVnp_Q","name":"vexa","full_name":"kovacsistvanpeter-stack/vexa","owner":{"login":"kovacsistvanpeter-stack","id":264636533,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8YIdQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/264636533?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack","html_url":"https://github.com/kovacsistvanpeter-stack","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kovacsistvanpeter-stack/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/u